e was badly flagging  but it's been very well revitalize din  recent years and Marvel kind of doing  this oh we wish we had the x-men well  what's the closest thing we got them  selves the rights to oh we can do the  Inhumans I don't like that because what  part of what's been great about marvel  all this is they are the leaders in this  movie comic book industry and the other  thing about the Inhumans if they use  them similar to how x-men gets use we're  now suddenly they can have a ton of  characters that they don't have to  justify where they got their powers from  that really does risk them flooding the  universe with too many super-powered  characters I mean let us not forget  they've had to cull the herd several  times in the comic books with the legacy  virus decimation they get overloaded  with these guys and it could very easily  happen in the movies if they're not  really careful about it let me be clear  I'm not saying Marvel's headed down the  wrong path of that their movie suddenly  suck I'm just saying that I'm noticing  these patterns that they worry me and  their patterns that I really want to see  Marvel either break away from her find a  way to subvert because if they keep  going down the path that they've set  it's gonna start to unravel on them but  I have a pretty good amount of faith in  them that they're well aware enough that  some of these things if not all of them  will get corrected but I just got to get  my feelings out there and my concerns  maybe you share them maybe you think I'm  crazy you know what at this point we've  got ten Marvel movies that have hit  theaters so out of the ten what is your  personal favorite Marvel movie drop  something down in the comments and let's  talk about it until next time this  council is adjourned

